{ Before examining any lines, it should be noted that 1.d4 c6 also makes it possible to play a version of the Queen's Gambit Accepted. }
1. d4 c6 2. c4 d5 3. Nf3 dxc4 { This is playable, but it's not part of this repertoire, as my approach to 1...c6 is based on ensuring that black achieves a solid position with equality or virtual equality, and dampening down any attempts from white to sharpen play. } *

