1. e4 c6 { The Caro-Kann defence begins with these moves. Black's aim is simple - to challenge the centre with 2...d5, regardless of white's second move.
White has several possible responses to the Caro-Kann, but many branch out from an initial 2. d4, so we will examine these possibilities first. } *

