{ 1. e4 and 1. d4 are collectively played in approximately 80% of chess games. But white has several other options available, and in this final section we're going to examine some of these. }
1. c4 { The fourth most popular opening move is 4. c4, but this requires particular attention with our 1...c6 repertoire, as English Opening players tend to be well-prepared, and there are several facets to this system that must be understood. } 1... c6 { Stockfish rates 1...c6 as marginally inferior to 1...c5 or 1...e5 here. But it's a practical response in our repertoire, as playing 1...e5 is effectively inviting a reverse Sicilian, while 1...c5 requires quite a bit of book knowledge.
With 1...c6, black will steer the game in a familiar direction. Here's how... } *

